        "detail": "彩绘檐口 · 文房四宝",
        "art": "Liulichang cultural street: distinguished traditional calligraphy and antiques storefronts with orderly rows of dark-gray Chinese tiled roofs, blue-green painted ornamental eaves, red wooden window lattice and a shop-window display of upright ink brushes, rolled blank scrolls and small inkstones. Detailed crafted facades with a quiet scholarly mood. Do not generate writing on scrolls or signs."
      },
      {
        "name": "陶然亭公园",
        "time": "14:40",
        "minutes": 80,
        "walk_after": 0,
        "detail": "湖畔秋色 · 慈悲庵古亭",
        "art": "Taoranting Park: a calm turquoise lake and the wooded island in the foreground, with Cibei Nunnery courtyard on the raised southwestern part of the island. Within the courtyard show the modest historic Taoran Pavilion, three-bay open rectangular hall with red wooden columns and a sober gray hip-and-gable roof on a white stone terrace. It belongs INSIDE this low temple courtyard, not a lone pavilion standing over water. Golden willow trees, the lake and one white stone island approach provide the surrounding park identity. Human-scale sober architecture, no Temple of Heaven or Summer Palace."
      }
